      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "An impressive three-bedroom terraced residence which has been extensively refurbished and extended to create a bright, contemporary home in this established and convenient Dundalk location.\n\nFinished to a very high standard throughout, No. 68 combines the character of the original property with a superb modern extension to the rear. The result is a surprisingly spacious home, with the standout feature being the large open-plan kitchen, dining and living area overlooking the rear garden.\n\nThe kitchen is fitted with an attractive range of shaker-style units, complemented by contemporary worktops, integrated oven and hob and excellent storage. High ceilings and rooflights bring an abundance of natural light into the extension, while double doors open directly onto the rear patio and garden, creating an excellent connection between the indoor and outdoor living spaces.\n\nThe accommodation also includes three well-proportioned bedrooms both finished in fresh neutral décor, together with a beautifully appointed modern bathroom featuring large-format marble-effect tiling, a glazed shower enclosure and chrome heated towel rail.\n\nExternally, the property benefits from an attractive, low-maintenance enclosed front garden with gated pedestrian access. To the rear is a particularly generous garden predominantly laid in lawn with a patio immediately outside the house. Its excellent depth provides ample space for outdoor dining, entertaining and family use.\n\nThe refurbishment has given the property a clean and contemporary finish throughout, while retaining a practical and easily maintained layout. The combination of the impressive rear extension, modern kitchen and bathroom, three bedrooms and substantial garden makes this a particularly appealing home for first-time buyers, downsizers and investors alike.\n\nSituated in Father Murray Park, the property enjoys an established residential setting within easy reach of Dundalk Town Centre and its extensive range of shops, schools, cafés, sporting facilities and everyday amenities. Transport connections are also readily accessible with Dundalk train and bus services and the M1 motorway providing convenient links to Dublin, Belfast and surrounding areas.\n\n68 Father Murray Park represents an excellent opportunity to acquire a comprehensively upgraded, ready-to-occupy home with exceptional living space and generous garden in a convenient Dundalk location.\n\nViewing is highly recommended."
      },
